joins :- A join is a query that combines rows from two or more tables , views, materialized view.
===> TYPES OF JOINS 
1. INNER JOIN -> matched data only
2. OUTER JOIN
3. SELF JOIN
4. CROSS JOIN
5. SEMI JOIN
6. ANTI JOIN

--> INNER JOIN:- INNER JOIN is used to combine two tables and return only the rows where the join condition matches. Non-matching rows are NOT included.
Inner join can be classified into two types.
I. Equi join:- Equi join is a type in inner join where tables are joined by equal(=) operator.
example:- select A.name,b.product from A INNER JOIN B on A.id = b.id
A,B-> tablename  | name, product,id -> columname 
II. NON Equi Join:- Non Equi join is a join where tables are joined other than equality such as >, <, >=, <=, BETWEEN.
example:- select A.id,B.id FROM A INNER JOIN B on A.value < B.value;
